// >>> win10-skin: the Windows 10 jump list skin <<<
//
// The jump lists, i.e. the menus which open when a taskbar button is
// right-clicked, are drawn by ShellExperienceHost.exe (and, on the builds which
// have one, by ShellHost.exe), so the Windows 10 look for them is a second
// skin, applied in those processes. It is the "10JumpLists" theme of the
// Windows 11 notification center styling guide, the only theme of that guide
// which this mod carries over.
//
// The styles target the jump-list UI only (JumpViewUI.*, its grid, acrylic
// borders and its own menu flyout parts). They do not restyle notification or
// toast content; selected native shell flyouts have a separate, independently
// gated style set below.
